<title>FRANCE: Henin Vie 96 profit jumps 72.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Henin Vie 96 profit jumps 72.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net					     25.6  vs		16</p>
<p>    Gross premiums	  (billion)	  5.5  up	  48 pct</p>
<p>Note - French life insurer La Henin Vie, 68 percent owned by Cie de Suez said in a statement that its big rise in 1996 net profit was due to strong productivity gains.</p>
<p>&quot;Barring unexpected events, 1997 should see another rise in profitability of the company,&quot; said La Henin Vie, saying that operations since the start of the year had been &quot;satisfactory.&quot;</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
